# The files of src/ that only the PostgreSQL extension compiles: they include server headers or call server APIs that the SQLite and MariaDB hosts do not provide. Every other file of
# src/ is in portable.list or portable-col.list (core/host.h only; scripts/check-portable.sh); scripts/check-classified.sh fails on a file that is in none of the three or in two.
# A line is a file, or a folder (ends with /) with every file below it. A portable file that calls into a file of this list gets the callee in the portable core or a function in sqlite/host
# (check-portable.sh links the SQLite build without undefined symbols).
